From 1b83b2e36831d73dc5ada91a80ac1f4ac402380b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 02:44:42 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 211/638] web_apps: add AROS file-handling guidance [chromium]
 [aros]

Statement:
The portable Web App settings controller exposes file-handling state on AROS, but its generic default-app guidance resource was restricted to Linux and Fuchsia.

Decision:
Admit AROS to the generic file-browser wording. It avoids naming a foreign desktop shell and accurately describes the browser-level capability.

Evidence:
The generated_resources GRIT actions regenerate for host and AROS, and web_app_settings_ui.o compiles.

Chain:
Completes the Web App settings resource admission from 824d5b1e56 for.
---
 chrome/app/app_management_strings.grdp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/chrome/app/app_management_strings.grdp b/chrome/app/app_management_strings.grdp
index f13044998e..32ba7cf294 100644
--- a/chrome/app/app_management_strings.grdp
+++ b/chrome/app/app_management_strings.grdp
@@ -202,7 +202,7 @@
       You can open and edit supported files with this app from Finder or other apps. To control which files open this app by default, <ph name="BEGIN_LINK">&lt;a href="#"&gt;</ph>learn how to set default apps on your device<ph name="END_LINK">&lt;/a&gt;</ph>.
     </message>
   </if>
-  <if expr="is_fuchsia or is_linux">
+  <if expr="is_fuchsia or is_linux or is_aros">
     <message name="IDS_APP_MANAGEMENT_FILE_HANDLING_SET_DEFAULTS_LINK" desc="Further explanation of the File Handling API, including text describing the purpose of the toggle (referencing a generic Linux file browser app) and a link to a learn more link for default filetype associations.">
       You can open and edit supported files with this app from your file browser or other apps. To control which files open this app by default, <ph name="BEGIN_LINK">&lt;a href="#"&gt;</ph>learn how to set default apps on your device<ph name="END_LINK">&lt;/a&gt;</ph>.
     </message>
